  "literature_notes": "Prestin (SLC26A5) has an intracellular N-terminus (residues 1\u201383) and an intracellular C-terminus (residues 502\u2013744); it has no extracellular terminus. Its seven extracellular loops are short (1\u201328 aa) and none of the ledger lines reports a tag inserted into any of them. L1 places a YFP at aa 28\u201330, which is deep in the intracellular N-terminus. L6 places GFP at the intracellular C-terminus (residue 744). L7\u2013L9 describe an HA-prestin construct whose HA tag is at the protein N-terminus, which is also intracellular; NLC was preserved, confirming functional expression, but the tag faces the cytoplasm. L10\u2013L13 describe a C-terminal 6\u00d7His tag, again intracellular. L2\u2013L5 describe a BAP-PDGFR-prestin-GFP chimera: the BAP biotin-acceptor peptide is surface-exposed, but it sits on the appended PDGFR single-pass domain, not on any loop of prestin itself; the authors explicitly state the construct was designed 'without altering the primary sequence of the prestin hydrophobic core'. No ledger line reports a tag inserted into any extracellular loop or extracellular face of full-length, membrane-anchored prestin. Zero sites qualify.",
